.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt PORTIA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm portia
.Nd AI-driven FreeBSD porter's assistant
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm new
.Ar category/port
.Nm
.Cm update
.Ar category/port
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a deterministic harness around a language model that automates the
mechanical parts of porting software to FreeBSD.
It does no porting itself: it owns the command, the target directory,
the prompt handed to the model, and the check that a port-shaped result
landed.
Only the porting work in the middle
\(em reading the distfile, matching dependencies, writing the Makefile
\(em is left to the model.
.Pp
Each command takes a single
.Ar category/port
origin, which must contain exactly one slash with non-empty halves.
The port is written to
.Pa category/port
beneath
.Ev PORTSDIR .
.Nm
creates that directory, hands the model the command's prompt together
with the origin and the target path, and then verifies the expected
port files landed there non-empty.
.Pp
.Ev PORTSDIR
must be a repository \(em the ports tree \(em managed by jj or git.
.Nm
prefers jj when both are present, so the commit can be named by a stable
jj change id rather than a git sha, and because a jj workspace has no
git directory of its own.
Once the expected files are present,
.Nm
commits the port with a message the model writes to a scratch file it
is handed.
The message follows the commit conventions of the surrounding tree and,
for an
.Cm update ,
cites the upstream changelog for every intermediate version.
The commit is the natural stopping point;
.Nm
refuses to run at all when
.Ev PORTSDIR
is under neither jj nor git.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width troubleshoot
.It Cm new Ar category/port
Create a new, complete port.
Free-form detail
.Pq version, home page, author, git repository
is read from standard input and passed to the model as context.
From it the model finds the distfile, determines the build system and
dependencies, mines the ports tree for prior art, and produces a
.Pa Makefile ,
a
.Pa distinfo ,
and a
.Pa pkg-descr .
.It Cm update Ar category/port
Bump an existing port to its newest upstream version.
The model raises the version, resets
.Va PORTREVISION ,
reconciles dependencies, and regenerates
.Pa distinfo
for the new distfile.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PORTSDIR
.It Ev MODEL
The model command, defaulting to
.Ql claude .
It is left unquoted at the call site, so additional words split into
separate arguments.
Because the model must be allowed to write files, invoke it with a
permission mode that permits edits:
.Pp
.Dl MODEL="claude --permission-mode acceptEdits" portia new www/foo
.It Ev PORTSDIR
The root of the ports tree, defaulting to the current directory.
It must be a jj or git repository; the port is written to
.Pa PORTSDIR/category/port
and committed there once verified.
When the tree is managed by both, the commit is made with jj.
.El
.Sh FILES
Relative to the port directory
.Pa PORTSDIR/category/port :
.Bl -tag -width pkg-descr
.It Pa Makefile
The port Makefile.
.It Pa distinfo
Distfile checksums and sizes, produced by
.Cm new
and
.Cm update .
.It Pa pkg-descr
A prose description of the software.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the model leaves every expected file non-empty in the port
directory and the port is committed.
It exits 64 when invoked with no command or no origin, and 1 when the
origin is malformed, a prompt cannot be read,
.Ev PORTSDIR
is under neither jj nor git, the model invocation fails, the model
returns without producing an expected file or a commit message, or the
commit fails.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a new port, feeding it detail on standard input:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
MODEL="claude --permission-mode acceptEdits" \e
    portia new www/foo <<-EOF
	version 1.2.3
	home page https://example.org/foo
	author A. Hacker
	git https://github.com/example/foo
EOF
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr jj 1 ,
.Xr sclr 1
.Sh CAVEATS
The porting work is performed by the model and is not guaranteed
correct.
.Nm
verifies only that the expected files were produced, not that the port
builds.
